course: dictionary
lesson: 6894
title: Overturn: turning things over
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one to use. «Jesus overturned the traders' tables in the Temple, saying, My house shall be a house of prayer.» Overturned means turned over, so the tables ended up upside down. The words around it are the clue: tables are things that get turned over, not things that get changed in a meeting.
explain: Overturn has two other meanings you will meet. A judge can overturn a ruling, which means officially changing it and saying it was wrong. Scientists can overturn an old idea when new evidence shows it is wrong or should be replaced. Ask yourself: is something physically turning over, or is a decision or idea being changed?
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Jesus turned over the traders' tables» still makes sense, so turn over is a good meaning here. If your swap made the sentence silly, try a different meaning.
fact: Overturn means to turn over, or make something turn over, so the bottom is on top.
fact: «Overturned» is the past tense: «The wind overturned the little boat» means the boat turned over.
fact: Overturn can also mean to officially change a decision and say it was wrong.
fact: To overturn an idea is to show it is wrong or to replace it with a better one.
fact: Overturn is a verb, so it changes: overturn, overturns, overturned, overturning.
exercise: «Jesus overturned the traders' tables in the Temple.» What does overturned mean here? | Counted one by one | Carefully cleaned | Painted in bright colours | *Turned over, so the bottom was on top
exercise: The judge overturned the ruling. What does overturned mean here? | Agreed with it and wrote it down | *Officially changed the decision and said it was wrong | Read it out loud to the court | Made a bigger fuss about it
exercise: «The wind overturned the little boat.» Which word is closest in meaning to overturned? | Polished | Stayed | Floated | *Toppled
test: Scientists found new evidence that can overturn an old idea. What does overturn mean here? | *Show the idea is wrong and replace it | Explain the idea to a friend | Write the idea in a book | Forget the idea on purpose
test: Which sentence uses overturn to mean turn over? | *The strong wind overturned the bin | The cat slept on the mat | The school bell rang at nine | She read a book about trains
exam: The council overturned the ban on bikes in the park, so bikes are allowed again. What does overturned mean here? | Turned upside down | *Officially changed and said to be wrong | Painted over | Hidden under a cloth
